  "term": "ADS model",
  "definition": "ADS model refers here to a computer-vision model for detecting and separating individual apples in orchard images, including apples that are partly hidden, overlapping, shadowed, or changing color as they grow. In this source, it is an improved Mask Scoring R-CNN approach designed for accurate, real-time apple detection and segmentation in natural conditions.",
